course: dictionary
lesson: 3843
title: Forward: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The robot moved forward one step.» Here forward means toward the front, in the direction you are facing. A step shows you that the robot is moving.
explain: «She had been looking forward to her great-aunt's visit for weeks.» Here forward means toward the future: she was excited about something still to come. To check, swap in a word like "ahead". "Looking ahead to her visit" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Forward can also be a verb: to forward a message is to send it on to someone else. In some sports, a forward is a player who attacks. Read the words around it, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Forward means toward the front, in the direction you are facing.
fact: Forward can mean toward the future, as in «look forward to» something.
fact: To forward a message is to send it on to someone else.
fact: A forward is a player who attacks in some sports.
fact: In British English, forward can also be written as forwards.
exercise: «Moving forward does not change which way it faces.» What does forward mean in this sentence? | *Toward the front, in the direction you are facing | Toward the future | Backwards | To send on to someone else
exercise: She had been «looking forward to it». What does looking forward mean here? | Looking at the front of the house | Looking back at the past | Forgetting all about it | *Waiting eagerly for something still to come
exercise: Dad says, «Please forward me the message.» What does forward mean? | *To send it on to someone else | To step to the front of the line | To read it slowly | To delete it without reading it
test: «He will forward the letter to Grandma.» Which meaning fits? | To carry it toward the front of the room | To write a brand-new letter | To look forward to reading it | *To send it on to someone else
test: «The team's forward ran straight at the goal.» What is a forward in this sentence? | *A player who attacks | A coach who shouts instructions | A player who guards the goal | A kind of football
exam: «Before you forward a message, think about who will read it.» Why should you think first? | Because forward means backwards | *Because it might reach people it was never meant for | Because forwarding always takes a long time | Because messages disappear when they are forwarded
